OL,3,CProgramme listings for SUN 28 DEC
OL,4,G1200FPrivate Passions
OL,5,     GMichael Berkeley's guest is the
OL,6,     Gactor and writer Rupert Everett,
OL,7,     Gwhose musical passions include
OL,8,     GHandel, Purcell, Wagner and
OL,9,     GMahler.
OL,10,G1330FMusic Map
OL,11,     GSara Mohr-Pietsch traces a path
OL,12,     Gtowards Rachmaninov's Rhapsody on
OL,13,     Ga Theme of Paganini, a single-
OL,14,     Gmovement work for piano and
OL,15,     Gorchestra, based on one of
OL,16,     GPaganini's Violin Caprices.
OL,17,G1500FChoral Evensong
OL,18,     GA service of Choral Evensong with
OL,19,     GCarols for Christmas Eve from St
OL,20,     GMartin-in-the-Fields, London,
OL,21,     Gwith music by Bob Chilcott and
OL,22,     GJohn Rutter.
